{"idx": 31, "output": "CQ number 9 for the dolce ontology is: Is [x] Atomic due to not having any proper parts?\n\nRelevant DOLCE axiom:  \n:Atom rdf:type owl:Class ;  \n      rdfs:subClassOf :Particular ,  \n                      [ owl:complementOf [ owl:onProperty [ owl:inverseOf :properPartOf ] ; owl:someValuesFrom :Particular ] ] .\n\nThis means that an individual is an instance of :Atom if and only if it does not have any proper parts (i.e., there does not exist a particular that is a proper part of it).", "label": "Is blank Atomic due to having no subdivisions and having a definite end point?", "prompt": "CQ number 9 for the dolce ontology is: Is blank Atomic due"}
{"idx": 32, "output": "CQ number 10 for the dolce ontology is: Is blank a location\n\nDOLCE answer pattern:  \nCheck if the individual referred to as \"blank\" is an instance of the class :SpatialLocation. If \"blank\" is an instance of :SpatialLocation, then \"blank\" is a location according to DOLCE.", "label": "Is blank a location of or occupied by some object?", "prompt": "CQ number 10 for the dolce ontology is: Is blank a location"}
{"idx": 33, "output": "CQ number 11 for the dolce ontology is: Is <X> a collection\n\nIn DOLCE, the notion of \"collection\" is not explicitly represented as a primitive class. However, collections can be modeled as particular kinds of endurants, typically as non-physical objects (such as a set, a group, or a collection of entities), or as social objects (such as a committee or a team), depending on the intended meaning.\n\nTo answer whether <X> is a collection in DOLCE, one would check if <X> is an instance of a class that represents a group, set, or aggregate entity, such as :NonPhysicalObject, :SocialObject, or a subclass thereof (e.g., :Society, :AgentiveSocialObject, :NonAgentiveSocialObject). If <X> is modeled as an instance of such a class, then <X> can be considered a collection in the sense of DOLCE.\n\nThus, the answer depends on the classification of <X> within the ontology, specifically whether it is an instance of a class representing a group or aggregate entity.", "label": "Is blank a collection of things, regardless of their spatial or other differences?", "prompt": "CQ number 11 for the dolce ontology is: Is blank a collection"}
