{"idx": 44, "output": "begin and end?\n\nA perdurant in the DOLCE ontology is an entity that happens in time, such as events, processes, or states. The temporal boundaries of a perdurant are determined by the unique time interval at which it is exactly located. This is represented in DOLCE by the property :temporallyLocatedAt, which relates a perdurant to a :TimeInterval.\n\nTherefore, a perdurant begins at the starting instant of its associated :TimeInterval and ends at the ending instant of that :TimeInterval. The specific time interval can be retrieved via the :temporallyLocatedAt property.", "label": "when does a perdurant A participate in another perdurant B by consequence of A being a part of endurant C", "prompt": "CQ number 22 for the dolce ontology is: when does a perdurant"}
